**Executable gate contract.** The compiled sibling gate snapshot is the resolved membership, prerequisites and selection contract. Check acceptance coverage against the immutable oracle; do not expand the roster from generic applicability rules.

**Authorized effects.** {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}

**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The samples suite becomes a contract suite that any samples store runs (001 §C 'Contract tests': each library proxy's suite runs against the in-memory store AND SQLite `:memory:`; .spec-md §9), as step 66 did for materials. This step moves facts and adds no store; every fact keeps its name and its assertions. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs`: `[<AbstractClass>] type SampleProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshProxy : unit -> SampleProxy`, a store holding the Built-in catalogue's samples, each at version 1, active and unpinned. `proxyWithPinned` (step 65) becomes a member over `freshProxy` that pins through `pinSampleVersion`. These 21 facts become `[<Fact>]` members of the contract: `listSamples ActiveOnly returns the seeded samples with distinct ids`; `searchSamples with the empty query matches every seeded sample`; `searchSamples filters by name fragment case-insensitively`; `searchSamples filters by substrate kind, composing with the text facet`; `tryGetSample hits a known id and misses a minted one`; `resolveVersion hits version 1 of a seed, misses a non-existent version, and misses an unknown id`; `saveSample on a new id inserts version 1 active — appears in listing and resolves at v1`; `saveSample rejects a blank name as InvalidSample and persists nothing`; `saveSample rejects a structurally-empty sample (no films, no substrate) as InvalidSample even when named`; `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged`; `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint`; `MutateInPlace — a structure change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place`; `MintNextVersion — a structure change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2`; `latest-active default listing shows one entry per sample after a mint, not the frozen history`; `markSampleInactive hides a sample from the offers yet keeps it resolvable, and markSampleActive revives it`; `supersedeSample behaves as inactive — hidden from offers, present under include-inactive, resolvable by version`; `the lifecycle verbs reject an unknown id with a diagnostic reason`; `removeSample on a sample with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version`; `removeSample succeeds when no version is pinned, then the id is unknown`; `a SampleProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)`; `pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`. `type SampleProxyTests () = inherit SampleProxyContract ()` is the in-memory store: `freshProxy` is `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore ()` (step 65). The facts over no samples store stay members of `SampleProxyTests` alone: `a Mirror's supportedEmission is unclearable: every candidate collapses to EmitReflectedOnly`; `a Plate is constrainable: clearing R via Emission.withReflected Placement.RayGroupOff leaves T on`; `a STUB SampleProxy over the versioned surface exercises every function through its exact signature`; `a sample layer keeps resolving its pinned material version after the material mints a newer one`; `defaultSupportedEmission pins a Mirror to EmitReflectedOnly; a ThinFilm and a Plate emit both`; `the seeded EUV multilayer is the one Mirror; seeded thin films and plates support both`; `validateSample accepts a Plate that carries a substrate and a non-blank name`; `validateSample leaves a ThinFilm with no substrate Ok`; `validateSample rejects a Plate whose structure.substrate is None as InvalidSample`. The values the facts share (`plate`, `otherStructure`, `platePhysicsChanged`, `plateRenamed`, `v1Id`, `v2Id`, `minted`, `emptyStructure`, `plateMissingSubstrate`) move unchanged into a private module above the classes. (2) The in-memory class keeps the name `SampleProxyTests`, so every fact keeps its id: xUnit v3 reports an inherited fact under the concrete class that runs it. The abstract contract holds no discoverable test of its own and gets no `ADD_TEST`. The file keeps its compile position, so no project file changes.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `SampleProxyContract` MUST be an abstract class holding the 21 store facts and `SampleProxyTests` its in-memory subclass; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged and every SampleProxyTests fact under its old id; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.
